/-! ## §1 — the deployed object: exactly what `EmitRotationV3.lean` prints for the key. -/

/-- **The DEPLOYED custom descriptor.** `EmitRotationV3.lean` iterates `v3RegistryCapOpenDep` and
prints `emitVmJson2 (dropUnforcedPins (hardenLastRow d))` for each `(key, d)`;
`customVmDescriptor2R24` is member 19 of the bare cohort, so `d` is
`withDfaRcPins (gentianDeployedBareRefuse customV3)` (`v3RegistryRefused`,
`EffectVmEmitRotationV3Refused.lean:39`). It is NOT in the emitter's `availOverride` list, so
nothing else rewrites it on the way out.

⚑ **THE TWO OUTERMOST WRAPPERS WERE MISSING HERE AND THE §2 PIN WAS THEREFORE PINNING AN OBJECT THE
EMITTER NEVER PRINTS.** `hardenLastRow` (every row-local `gate` lifted off the transition domain)
and `UnforcedPiPins.dropUnforcedPins` (the pins whose column no non-pin constraint reads — 14 of
them on THIS member) are applied by the emit driver, outermost, and both change the bytes. The
golden below is now the emitted string character-for-character; measured, not assumed. -/
def deployedCustomV3 : EffectVmDescriptor2 :=
  dropUnforcedPins (hardenLastRow (Dregg2.Circuit.Emit.FieldsCanonicity9Emit.fieldsCanonical9Wire
    (withDfaRcPins (gentianDeployedBareRefuse customV3))))

/-- **THE COMMITTED BYTES** — `circuit/descriptors/rotation-v3-staged-registry.tsv`, the row keyed
`customVmDescriptor2R24`, column 3, verbatim. This is the string Rust `include_str!`s and tab-scans
(`effect_vm_descriptors.rs::V3_STAGED_REGISTRY_TSV`), and the string `scripts/emit_descriptors.py`
`split_rotation` wrote there from the Lean emitter's stdout.

⚑ **RE-EMITTED 2026-07-31 at the rc-FOLD flag day**, and at the same time repaired in a second way:
the string was the 178-limb emission (`trace_width` 1672, `main` arity 1619) AND was the emit
driver's INPUT rather than its OUTPUT — `hardenLastRow` and `dropUnforcedPins` ride outermost and
both move the bytes, so this pin could not have matched the TSV even after the width fix. Both are
closed: `deployedCustomV3` now names the emitted object and this string is its `emitVmJson2`,
character for character. If a regen moves it again the §2 `#guard` goes RED — that red is the pin
DOING ITS JOB; re-emit and paste, never relax. -/
